In article <1992Feb6.787.4789@dosgate> john.russell@canrem.UUCP (John Russell) writes:
>Along the same lines, is there a list of shopkeeper names and their
>translations?  I still run into shopkeepers whose names I can't remember
>seeing before, and sometimes it takes a while before I can "translate"
>their names.
The name depends on the shoptype and the dungeonlevel. That is why you get so
often "Possogronoe", because that is a general store on level 2.
Most of the names comes from all kinds of cultures. The ringsshops are Dutch
but I do not recognize modern Dutch names. Maybe this should be changed.

The names of hardware-stores are names of the creators backwards like
"Kachzi Rellim" on level 15 (Izchak Miller).

>I still don't know what "Possogronoe" means, and it was
"Possogronoe" should be a name in Suriname, but it is also a little town in
Suriname (I found it on a very global map).

